### AWS IAM Policy Requirements

**Minimum IAM Policy for Kafka Consumer**

The following IAM policy grants minimum required permissions for a .NET application to consume from AWS MSK using IAM authentication.

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "MSKClusterAccess",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "kafka-cluster:Connect",
        "kafka-cluster:DescribeCluster"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kafka:us-east-1:123456789012:cluster/your-msk-cluster/*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "MSKTopicReadAccess",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "kafka-cluster:ReadData",
        "kafka-cluster:DescribeTopic"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kafka:us-east-1:123456789012:topic/your-msk-cluster/*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "MSKConsumerGroupAccess",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "kafka-cluster:AlterGroup",
        "kafka-cluster:DescribeGroup"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kafka:us-east-1:123456789012:group/your-msk-cluster/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

**IAM Role Configuration for EKS Pod**

For applications running in Amazon EKS, use IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA):

```yaml
# ServiceAccount with IAM role annotation
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: kafka-consumer-sa
  namespace: my-application
  annotations:
    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/my-app-kafka-consumer-role
```

**Terraform Example for IAM Policy**

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_policy" "kafka_consumer_policy" {
  name        = "kafka-consumer-policy"
  description = "Allows Kafka consumer access to MSK cluster"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid    = "MSKClusterAccess"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "kafka-cluster:Connect",
          "kafka-cluster:DescribeCluster"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:kafka:${var.aws_region}:${var.aws_account_id}:cluster/${var.msk_cluster_name}/*"
      },
      {
        Sid    = "MSKTopicReadAccess"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "kafka-cluster:ReadData",
          "kafka-cluster:DescribeTopic"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:kafka:${var.aws_region}:${var.aws_account_id}:topic/${var.msk_cluster_name}/*"
      },
      {
        Sid    = "MSKConsumerGroupAccess"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "kafka-cluster:AlterGroup",
          "kafka-cluster:DescribeGroup"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:kafka:${var.aws_region}:${var.aws_account_id}:group/${var.msk_cluster_name}/*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "kafka_consumer_attach" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.kafka_consumer_role.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.kafka_consumer_policy.arn
}
```

**Required AWS SDK Configuration**

Ensure AWS credentials are available via one of these methods:
- **EKS IRSA** (Recommended for production)
- **EC2 Instance Profile** (For EC2-based deployments)
- **Environment variables** (For local development only)

```csharp
// AWS SDK automatically discovers credentials from:
// 1. Environment variables (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY)
// 2. IAM role (EKS IRSA or EC2 instance profile)
// 3. Shared credentials file (~/.aws/credentials)

// No explicit credential configuration needed in code
// The Confluent.Kafka library will use AWS SDK's default credential chain
```

